  <li>PostgreSQL 18: <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-connection.html">Connections and Authentication</a>, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-wal.html">Write Ahead Log settings</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/backup-dump.html">SQL Dump</a>, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/transaction-iso.html">Transaction Isolation</a>, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/ddl-constraints.html">Constraints</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/queries-with.html">WITH queries</a>. <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/about/licence/">The PostgreSQL Licence</a> defines the engine’s permission terms.</li>
  <li>SQLite: <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/whentouse.html">Appropriate Uses For SQLite</a> and <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html">Write-Ahead Logging</a>, particularly same-host access and single-writer coordination.</li>
  <li>Amazon RDS: <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Concepts.MultiAZSingleStandby.html">Multi-AZ DB instance deployments</a>, <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Appendix.PostgreSQL.CommonDBATasks.Roles.rds_superuser.html">The rds_superuser role</a> and <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_UpgradeDBInstance.PostgreSQL.html">PostgreSQL engine upgrades</a>. These document a comparison; a selected tier and its acceptance evidence remain outstanding.</li>
  <li>CockroachDB 26.3: <a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.3/multiregion-overview">Multi-Region Capabilities Overview</a>, for distinguishing locality and survival goals before the conditional candidate evaluation.</li>
 </ul>
